["<task-notification>\n<task-id>a18afa5a1ae51b3f8</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01UzCjhneAZRRSMZ48WcTN9B</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/a18afa5a1ae51b3f8.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Write UI Toolkit design spec\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>The UI spec is written and committed as `29ec9d5` on `feature/ui-spec`. The spike answered all four questions; the one gap is that real keystrokes were not tested, only synthesized events. Nothing was left half-done when the rate limit hit, and no Unity runs are still going.\n\n**Gate check:** the spec cites 22 source URLs (8 required), and each one is marked in the spec as read or as seen only in a search summary. I looked at the spike screenshots myself with Read. `git status` is clean, and the commit only touches `docs/specs/ui.md` (new) and one index line in `docs/README.md`. No game code changed, and the spike code and scratch copy stayed outside git.\n\n**Key decisions in the spec:**\n- **Art direction (\"烛火手稿\" / Candlelit Codex):** warm near-black backgrounds, parchment-colored text, one ember-gold accent and thin bronze borders. The Kenney cartoon wood textures are dropped as the main look. The spec includes full color tokens with contrast ratios, plus a type scale, 4px spacing grid, corner and elevation rules, motion timings and sound cues.\n- **Rarity:** one ladder T0–T4 (普通 / 精良 / 稀有 / 史诗 / 传说), where the same Chinese name always gets the same color. Today the code disagrees: \"稀有\" is blue for items but gold for equipment. Equipment Magic changes blue→green and equipment Rare changes gold→blue. 独特 (unique) uses the 传说 color plus a decorated frame, because red is reserved for danger.\n- **Scaling:** design at 1920×1080, scaling with screen height. Layouts must also hold at 16:10 widths.\n- **Architecture:** one PanelSettings, one UIDocument with layer containers, screens built in C# plus USS (no UXML for now), and a component library of `VisualElement` subclasses. Each feature gets a thin view class that binds its existing model (Pause, Talent, Equipment models already exist with tests).\n- **Input:** the project uses only the legacy Input Manager, with no Input System or uGUI package. UI Toolkit's built-in event system works without any extra package or EventSystem. The catch is that WASD, Space and Esc are also UI navigate/submit/cancel keys, so only modal screens may hold focus, and focus is cleared when a screen closes.\n- **Migration order:**\n  - U0: foundation and a component gallery screen.\n  - U1: talent tree, built directly in UI Toolkit since it is being redesigned anyway; edges are drawn with `Painter2D`.\n  - U2: hub, equipment and merchant panels.\n  - U3: pause menu.\n  - U4: character sheet, bag and result screen.\n  - U5: boon pick and boss intro/death.\n  - U6: combat HUD, with performance gates.\n  - U7: delete IMGUI.\n  - Rollback is a per-feature `AGENT_UI_LEGACY` setting, so no revert is needed.\n- **Other docs:** the spec lists what must change in `progression-unified.md` §6 (the line ~367 IMGUI note, the screenshot line ~374, the Tab-key handling) and in `overview.md` line 15.\n\n**Spike results:**\n\n| Question | Result |\n|---|---|\n| (a) Chinese text | Renders correctly, both through the USS font setting and through a font asset created in code. Two flaws showed up: at 720p a line can start with \"，\" (line-break rules need configuring in U0), and Unity's default ProgressBar is nearly invisible, so the spec uses a custom bar. |\n| (b) Headless screenshot | Works with `-batchmode` alone: the UI renders into a RenderTexture and is blended onto the camera image. Checked at 1280×720 and 1920×1080. With `-nographics` it fails: the UI readback is uninitialized memory and `Camera.Render()` crashes (exit code 139). Screenshot runs must drop `-nographics`; a windowed run isn't needed. |\n| (c) Focus and input | Focus, arrow navigation, submit and pointer click all reach the right button without an EventSystem. These were events fired from code, because batch mode has no real keyboard. |\n| (d) Animation while paused | With `timeScale` at 0, `Time.time` stayed frozen while USS transitions finished in about 1 s of real time and the UI scheduler kept ticking. |\n\nThe spike evidence is in `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/scratchpad/uispec-spike/` (`gfx.log`, `nogfx.log`, `shots/gfx/*.png`). Scratch files may be cleaned up later; the spec's appendix A copies the measurements and the key code.\n\n**Still unverified (U0 must test these in a windowed run):**\n- Whether real key presses behave the same as the synthesized events.\n- Whether UI Toolkit reads keys before or after the existing key drivers and their `Input.ResetInputAxes()`, so one key isn't handled twice.\n- Whether IMGUI or UI Toolkit draws on top when both are on screen.\n- Whether this Unity version supports `line-height` or `box-shadow` in USS.\n- Primary sources for Hades and Dead Cells HUD layouts. Two pages returned 403, so those claims are flagged as coming from search summaries.\n\n**Open questions for you (my recommendation in brackets):**\n1. Do you accept the Candlelit Codex direction? [Yes; review the U0 gallery screenshots before starting U1.]\n2. Can the item and talent icons come from game-icons.net? Its CC BY 3.0 licence requires crediting authors, unlike the all-CC0 assets so far. [Yes; it only needs a credits file and an in-game credits page.]\n3. Is it OK to change two equipment rarity colors? [Yes.]\n4. Should the talent tree go first rather than the hub? [Yes.]\n5. Gamepad UI navigation now? [Not yet.]</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>238949</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>4</tool_uses><duration_ms>38422</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"]
